{# 
HOME — AGENCY-CALIBER INTERACTIVE CONCEPT — Award-winning Digital Creative Director + 3D Art Director
====================================================================================================
Visual Narrative:
Woodex is not a decorator. It is a Design + Build practice that draws a room so it can be built. The narrative is "DRAWN. THEN BUILT." — from plan to still to site. Every section moves from abstract (idea) to concrete (material). The user journeys from seeing to understanding to approving to building.

Art Direction:
Cinematic but quiet. No stock gradients. Real materials as heroes: walnut, brushed brass, poured concrete, fluted glass, boucle. Lighting is soft studio, 3200K key + 5600K fill, subtle AO. Composition uses 12-col grid, 1240px container, 24px gap, but breaks grid intentionally with giant bleed WOODEX 14rem 0.06 opacity. Depth via 3 layers: background (concrete), mid (wood), foreground (brass detail).

Typography:
Syne 600 for display (distinctive, architectural, not overused Plus Jakarta), Sora 400/600 for body (humanist, readable). H1 clamp 2.8-4.8rem -0.03em 1.05, H2 clamp 1.8-2.6rem -0.02em 1.2, eyebrow 11px 0.12em uppercase 600. Tight-leading fixed to 1.2+ for body, 1.05 for hero impact.

Color Palette:
Navy #0c1628 (ink, header), #0f1e36 (primary), Cream #fcf2e8 (air, Linoxa), #f4efe7 (warm), Charcoal #525252 (body), Wood #b8956a (accent, but used as brass not wood for contrast), White #fff. No fake gradients. All dark sections use white 0.7 for secondary to ensure 4.5:1.

Composition:
12-col, but each section breaks differently: Hero 6/6 split with layered depth, Services 7/5 with tilt image, Sectors 4/4/4 with icons, Stats 3/3/3/3 dark, Materials 6x 2-col, Process 7 gates snap 300px, Projects masonry 8/4 + 4/4/4, Wellstar 5/7 split, CTA 60/40.

Materials:
Walnut (hero side table), Concrete (hero overlay, trust bar), Brass (button icon circle, sector number), Glass (fluted glass in materials section), Boucle (soft seating), Stone (project plinths). Each material has its own light response: wood warm, concrete matte, brass specular.

Lighting:
Hero: softbox top-left 45deg, 3200K warm, falloff 70%. Services image: studio softbox + rim light. Materials: each card has its own HDRI — wood warm, concrete cool, brass highlight. No harsh shadows, only 0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.12) soft.

Atmosphere:
Calm, precise, confident. No bounce easing, only cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1) — Linoxa ease. No autoplay marquee, only static grid. No generic lorem, only client-driven language: CEO, Admin, HR, Procurement.

Depth:
Parallax: hero layers move on mouse (0.02, 0.05, 0.08). Tilt: cards tilt 8deg on mouse. Shadows: layered. Z: background 1, content 3, nav 50, giant bleed 2 with mask. Scroll progress bar top 2px navy.

Emotional Journey:
1. Arrival: Hero — first 10 seconds judgment, brand statement
2. Proof: Trust — 10y 200+ ISO Wellstar — proof before claim
3. Understanding: Services — what you can actually buy, not cloned cards
4. Seeing: 3D Studio Pin — see room before it exists, still is meeting
5. Belonging: Sectors — do you understand my business? 6 distinct visitors
6. Confidence: Stats + Materials — mill connected to still
7. Clarity: Process 7 gates — stop at gate you choose
8. Desire: Projects — studies drawn so they can be built
9. Trust: Wellstar — named client, not fake wall
10. Action: CTA — tell us about your space, next gate not brochure

Every decision intentional, distinctive, premium. Avoid generic templates.
#}
